sec.p:
For the distance of AMPAR to PSD-95/Homer1, a minimum centroid to centroid distance of 100 nm first finds pairs of AMPAR and PSD-95/Homer clusters. The distance between the two clusters is then calculated along their third principal component analysis (PCA) component directions (direction they orient toward each other). The 3D paired cross-correlation function (PCF) between two clusters is calculated using the formula below.13


gc(r→)=Re{FFT−1(FFT(I1)×conj[FFT(I2)])ρ1ρ2FFT−1(FFT(W1)×conj[FFT(W2)])
\begin{document}$$\displaystyle g_{c}(\vec{r})=\operatorname{Re}\left\{\frac{\operatorname{FFT}^{-1}\left(\operatorname{FFT}\left(I_{1}\right) \times \operatorname{conj}\left[\operatorname{FFT}\left(I_{2}\right)\right]\right)}{\rho_{1} \rho_{2} \operatorname{FFT}^{-1}\left(\operatorname{FFT}\left(W_{1}\right) \times \operatorname{conj}\left[\operatorname{FFT}\left(W_{2}\right)\right]\right)}\right.$$\end{document}
